title: Rueckfall: ein Programm, das sich nicht in Module teilen laesst (es erklaert eine Klasse der Prelude neu, und die Bibliothek von core im Cache hat die ihre), wird mit linkage source gebaut und sagt es
# (the check of the interface in the cache: the classes of the module core there are not those of this program - LinkageTests built the CLI program into the
#  same cache before; with an empty cache core is built for this program, and that is right, too)
needs: gcc
env FIRE_NATIVE_CACHE=$OUT/cache
sh mkdir -p $OUT/first $OUT/static $OUT/fresh && printf 'print("first")\n' > $OUT/first.fire
forge build own.fire --engine native --toolchain gcc --linkage static -o $OUT/fresh/own
lacks "not possible"
run $OUT/fresh/own
expect-text "caught x\n"
sh rm -rf $OUT/cache
forge build $OUT/first.fire --engine native --toolchain gcc --linkage static -o $OUT/first/first
forge bytecode own.fire -o $OUT/own.fbc
vm $OUT/own.fbc
expect-text "caught x\n"
forge build own.fire --engine native --toolchain gcc --linkage static -o $OUT/static/own
contains "not possible"
contains "declares classes of the module anew"
run $OUT/static/own
expect-text "caught x\n"
